@startuml
title PATCH /api/v1/games/{game_id}
hide footbox
actor Client
participant "FastAPI / Pydantic" as API
participant "SQLAlchemy session" as DB
database PostgreSQL as PG
Client -> API: PATCH /api/v1/games/{game_id}
API -> API: Validate path, query and body
note over API: Invalid input -> 422
No authentication required
API -> DB: get_db(): request transaction
DB -> PG: Lock game FOR UPDATE; missing -> 404
DB -> PG: Apply date_played if supplied
DB -> PG: If players supplied: reject any existing result (409)
DB -> PG: If players supplied: delete old players; flush
DB -> PG: If players supplied: validate/lock same-pod members; insert replacements
DB -> PG: Flush and load players plus nullable result
PG --> DB: Rows / mutation outcome
DB --> API: Route result
API -> API: Validate/serialize response
API -> DB: Finish successful request
DB -> PG: COMMIT
API --> Client: 200
note over API, PG: Any failure aborts the success path and rolls back.
See transaction.puml for shared error handling.
@enduml
